{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "id": "kukhnya-s01e01-scene-05",
 "pair": "ru-en",
 "title": "Мечта о кухне  (Dream of the Kitchen)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "max": "Макс",
  "nagiyev": "Нагиев"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "This scene steps back to Max's army days, when he cooked in a military kitchen. He starts by telling us he always knew he'd be a cook, and then the famous owner of Claude Monet, Nagiyev, drops by, tastes his soup and makes him an offer. Here it is in Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я всегда знал, что буду поваром.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Не пожарным и не космонавтом.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Даже не президентом. А именно поваром.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Вот он, наш герой!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Мне очень понравилась ваша солянка.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Спасибо! Я очень старался.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Молодец. Из ничего практически шедевр.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Хотите поработать в хорошем ресторане?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Конечно! Это моя мечта.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Милости просим. Буду рад.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Я говорю совершенно серьёзно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "В каком ресторане?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ресторан Клод Моне в Москве.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Спасибо огромное! Я обязательно приду.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's go through it slowly.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я всегда знал, что буду поваром.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I always knew I would be a chef.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "знал",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " ends in a masculine ending because Max is a man. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "буду поваром",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"I will be a cook\", and the word for \"cook\" has the same \"as a\" ending as before.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Не пожарным и не космонавтом.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Not a firefighter and not an astronaut.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Не",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "... ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "и не",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the Russian \"neither this nor that\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "пожарным",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " has the word for a fire inside it, and both jobs end in the \"as a\" endings.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Даже не президентом. А именно поваром.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Not even president. Exactly a chef.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Даже не",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"not even\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "именно",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means \"precisely\", and Russians put it right before the thing they want to underline.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Вот он, наш герой!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Here he is, our hero!' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Вот",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the pointing word, \"here is\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Вот он",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"here he is\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "наш",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", \"our\", is what makes the cook sound like one of the family.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Мне очень понравилась ваша солянка.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I really liked your solyanka.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "понравилась",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the past of the \"pleasing\" verb from the bar, with a prefix in front to make it \"took a liking\". It takes a feminine ending because ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "солянка",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", a thick sour soup, is a feminine word, and the soup is what did the pleasing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Спасибо! Я очень старался.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Thank you! I tried very hard.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "старался",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means to try, to make an effort. In the past it ends with a masculine ending for a man, and a feminine ending for a woman, so you can tell a lot about the speaker from one letter.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Молодец. Из ничего практически шедевр.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Well done. Practically a masterpiece out of nothing.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Молодец",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is what you say to someone who did well, and it comes from the word for young. It's used for women too. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Из ничего",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is literally \"out of nothing\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Хотите поработать в хорошем ресторане?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Would you like to work in a good restaurant?' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Хотите",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the formal \"you want\", right for an owner talking to a young cook he's only just met. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "поработать",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"to work for a while\": here the prefix adds \"a bit\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Конечно! Это моя мечта.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Of course! That is my dream.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Конечно",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is spelled with a \"ch\" but pronounced with an \"sh\" sound. Remember that one. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "моя мечта",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"my dream\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "моя",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the feminine \"my\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Милости просим. Буду рад.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You are welcome. I will be glad.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Милости просим",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is a warm old phrase, literally \"we ask for your kindness\", and it means \"welcome\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Буду рад",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"I will be glad\", the future of \"to be\" plus the word for \"glad\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Я говорю совершенно серьёзно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I am speaking completely seriously.' Nagiyev stacks two adverbs, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "совершенно",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", completely, and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "серьёзно",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", seriously. Both end in a vowel, which is how many Russian adjectives become \"-ly\" words: the word for \"serious\" turns into the word for \"seriously\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "В каком ресторане?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'In which restaurant?' It's the same ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "В каком ресторане",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " as in the night-time talk, with the words taking their endings after \"in\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ресторан Клод Моне в Москве.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Restaurant Claude Monet in Moscow.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "в Москве",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"in Moscow\", and now the name takes a new ending after \"in\". When it meant \"of Moscow\" it ended differently.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Спасибо огромное! Я обязательно приду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Thank you very much! I will definitely come.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "огромное",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means \"huge\", so ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Спасибо огромное",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"huge thanks\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "приду",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the future of \"come\", with no \"will\" in front. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я всегда знал, что буду поваром.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Не пожарным и не космонавтом.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Даже не президентом. А именно поваром.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Вот он, наш герой!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Мне очень понравилась ваша солянка.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Спасибо! Я очень старался.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Молодец. Из ничего практически шедевр.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Хотите поработать в хорошем ресторане?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Конечно! Это моя мечта.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Милости просим. Буду рад.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Я говорю совершенно серьёзно.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "В каком ресторане?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ресторан Клод Моне в Москве.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Спасибо огромное! Я обязательно приду.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "One bowl of soup, and Max has a job offer from a restaurant owner he'd only seen on television. Keep an ear out for \"my dream\" and \"of course\", because you'll hear both again.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "До встречи!",
   "gap": 0.3
  }
 ],
